    "final_selection_reason": "1) Strongest intrinsic metrics: Iteration 2. It has the highest silhouette (0.0757), the lowest WC-dispersion and Banfield\u2013Raftery scores; although its Davies\u2013Bouldin index is higher than Iterations 0/1, the overall intrinsic profile is strongest. 2) Most reasonable cluster structure: Iteration 2. It yields 11 clusters with balanced sizes, only two very small clusters (\u224831-cell dendritic and 14-cell platelet populations), and no dominant cluster; Iteration 0 has an extra tiny cluster, suggesting slightly more fragmentation. 3) Strongest biological interpretation: Iteration 2. It recovers all major PBMC populations with coherent markers\u2014naive/memory CD4 T (IL7R, LTB, SELL), B cells (CD79A/B, MS4A1, HLA class II), CD14+ monocytes (LYZ, S100A8/A9, FCN1), FCGR3A+ monocytes (LST1, FCGR3A), distinct cytotoxic/NK states (NKG7, GNLY, GZMB/PRF1; FGFBP2/GZMH), a clear GZMK+ CD8 T subset (GZMK, CCL5, HOPX), an interferon-stimulated module (ISG15, IFI6, IFIT1) of non-tiny size, dendritic cells (FCER1A, HLA-DP/A), and platelets (PF4, PPBP). Iteration 1 likely merges the IFN-stimulated subset; Iteration 0 captures it but as a very small cluster. 4) Ultimately selected: Iteration 2. 5) Trade-off: Although Iteration 2\u2019s Davies\u2013Bouldin index is worse than Iterations 0/1, its superior silhouette, WC-dispersion, and Banfield\u2013Raftery\u2014together with clearer separation of known PBMC subpopulations (including IFN-stimulated and GZMK+ CD8 T, and plausible NK sub-states) with minimal tiny clusters\u2014provide the strongest overall evidence.",
